{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"DOI:\"10.1038/s41467-025-64002-z\"","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"41062467","source":"MED","pmid":"41062467","pmcid":"PMC12508460","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC12508460"]},"doi":"10.1038/s41467-025-64002-z","title":"Structural insights into the mechanism of activation and inhibition of the prostaglandin D2 receptor 1.","authorString":"Davoudinasab B, Raskovalov A, Lee W, Kim D, Kim H, Lam JH, Han GW, Katritch V, Cherezov V.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Davoudinasab B","firstName":"Behnaz","lastName":"Davoudinasab","initials":"B","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0008-1425-3902"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Chemistry, University of Southern California, Los Angeles, CA, USA."},{"affiliation":"Bridge Institute, University of Southern California, Los Angeles, CA, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Raskovalov A","firstName":"Aleksey","lastName":"Raskovalov","initials":"A","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1207-5312"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Chemistry, University of Southern California, Los Angeles, CA, USA."},{"affiliation":"Bridge Institute, University of Southern California, Los Angeles, CA, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Lee W","firstName":"Woojin","lastName":"Lee","initials":"W","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8531-0301"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Bridge Institute, University of Southern California, Los Angeles, CA, USA."},{"affiliation":"Department of Quantitative and Computational Biology, University of Southern California, Los Angeles, CA, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Kim D","firstName":"Donggyun","lastName":"Kim","initials":"D","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Chemistry, University of Southern California, Los Angeles, CA, USA."},{"affiliation":"Bridge Institute, University of Southern California, Los Angeles, CA, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Kim H","firstName":"Heesoo","lastName":"Kim","initials":"H","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biological Sciences, University of Southern California, Los Angeles, CA, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Lam JH","firstName":"Jordy Homing","lastName":"Lam","initials":"JH","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-5496-6228"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Bridge Institute, University of Southern California, Los Angeles, CA, USA."},{"affiliation":"Department of Quantitative and Computational Biology, University of Southern California, Los Angeles, CA, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Han GW","firstName":"Gye Won","lastName":"Han","initials":"GW","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Bridge Institute, University of Southern California, Los Angeles, CA, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Katritch V","firstName":"Vsevolod","lastName":"Katritch","initials":"V","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-3883-4505"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Chemistry, University of Southern California, Los Angeles, CA, USA. katritch@usc.edu."},{"affiliation":"Bridge Institute, University of Southern California, Los Angeles, CA, USA. katritch@usc.edu."},{"affiliation":"Department of Quantitative and Computational Biology, University of Southern California, Los Angeles, CA, USA. katritch@usc.edu."},{"affiliation":"Center for New Technologies in Drug Discovery and Development, University of Southern California, Los Angeles, CA, USA. katritch@usc.edu."}]}},{"fullName":"Cherezov V","firstName":"Vadim","lastName":"Cherezov","initials":"V","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-5265-3914"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Chemistry, University of Southern California, Los Angeles, CA, USA. cherezov@usc.edu."},{"affiliation":"Bridge Institute, University of Southern California, Los Angeles, CA, USA. cherezov@usc.edu."},{"affiliation":"Center for New Technologies in Drug Discovery and Development, University of Southern California, Los Angeles, CA, USA. cherezov@usc.edu."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1207-5312"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-5265-3914"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-5496-6228"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8531-0301"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-3883-4505"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0008-1425-3902"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"1","volume":"16","journalIssueId":4025269,"dateOfPublication":"2025 Oct","monthOfPublication":10,"yearOfPublication":2025,"printPublicationDate":"2025-10-01","journal":{"title":"Nature communications","medlineAbbreviation":"Nat Commun","isoabbreviation":"Nat Commun","essn":"2041-1723","issn":"2041-1723","nlmid":"101528555"}},"pubYear":"2025","pageInfo":"8944","abstractText":"The prostaglandin D2 receptor 1 (DP1), a member of the prostanoid G protein-coupled receptor (GPCR) family, plays critical roles in allergic responses, sleep regulation, immune modulation, and vasodilation. Here, we present five high-resolution cryo-electron microscopy (cryo-EM) structures of the human DP1 receptor, including an apo structure, two inactive state structures bound to two different inverse agonists developed by ONO Pharmaceutical, and two active state structures in complex with the G<sub>s</sub> protein and bound to the endogenous agonist PGD2 and its selective derivative BW245C. Structural analysis, complemented by molecular dynamics simulations and site-directed mutagenesis, reveals key residues involved in ligand recognition and suggests a distinct activation mechanism for DP1, which lacks most of the conserved class A GPCR motifs. Notably, the unique residue K76 within the conserved sodium pocket acts as a major activation switch, while amphiphilic helix 8 adopts an unconventional orientation essential for receptor function. These findings offer valuable insights into the structure and function of prostanoid receptors and may facilitate the development of therapeutics targeting DP1.","affiliation":"Department of Chemistry, University of Southern California, Los Angeles, CA, USA.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"grantId":"U24 GM129541","agency":"NIGMS NIH HHS","acronym":"GM","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"R35 GM127086","agency":"NIGMS NIH HHS","acronym":"GM","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"R35GM153437","agency":"U.S. Department of Health & Human Services | NIH | National Institute of General Medical Sciences (NIGMS)","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"R35GM153437","agency":"U.S. Department of Health &amp; Human Services | NIH | National Institute of General Medical Sciences","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"R35 GM153437","agency":"NIGMS NIH HHS","acronym":"GM","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"R35GM127086","agency":"U.S. Department of Health &amp; Human Services | NIH | National Institute of General Medical Sciences","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"R35GM127086","agency":"U.S. Department of Health & Human Services | NIH | National Institute of General Medical Sciences (NIGMS)","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Prostaglandin D2","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Receptors, Prostaglandin","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"AI","qualifierName":"antagonists & inhibitors","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics","majorTopic_Y